    'JPG compression is lossy. It makes a file smaller by throwing away fine detail that the eye is least likely to miss, and the quality number decides how much is thrown away. A lower number gives a smaller file, but past a certain point you start to see blocky patches, smeared textures and faint halos around sharp edges. The detail that was removed cannot be brought back later, so always keep your original file.',
