    'First, the honest part. Converting a JPG to a PNG does not make the picture sharper or restore anything. The PNG stores exactly the pixels the JPG shows, including any blocky patches or soft edges that JPG compression left behind. The file also gets bigger, often several times bigger, because PNG has to record every pixel exactly.',
