    'That last point causes a common misunderstanding. The conversion itself does not remove the background. A JPG has a solid picture from edge to edge, and the PNG you get has the same solid picture. Making the background transparent is a separate editing step in a photo editor or a background remover.',
    'When should you not convert? When the goal is better quality, a smaller file or an image for a web page. In all three cases the JPG you already have is the better file. And when you finish editing a PNG and want to send it to someone, exporting a JPG copy for sharing will save them a large download.',
